Z||000006||VISCERAL||05-15-2000||10:08 AM||||87 Fiero GT -- only pic laying around<BR>STOCK 2.8<BR>MAGNECOR WIRES, K&N FILTER, SYNTHETIC OIL,<BR>CENTERFORCE II kevlar clutch, Grand am brakes all around, new steering rack, koni adjustables all around, rear coil over kit, suspension tech. lowering springs in front, 195 stat, header wrap, poly'd out cradle and suspension, rear addco sway bar, ride is harsh as hell on a bad road. Corners like a dream on smooth roads, but the everyday handling sucks over bad surfaces, no lift and surefooted at triple digit speed. <P>awaiting drop spindles and stock springs in front with a whole balljoint-tie rod revamp, and 17" or 18" wheels/tires. In fall V-8<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image0012.jpg"> ||||reg||1
